WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.767
- Are you okay, are
you stressed right now?

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.236
- I'm stressed out, I don't know!

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.627
What if she doesn't like it?

00:00:04.627 --> 00:00:08.210
- Yeah, that is gonna
reflect poorly on me.

00:00:09.096 --> 00:00:11.215
- [Both] It's Valentine's Day!

00:00:11.215 --> 00:00:14.303
- The worst holiday of
the year for everyone.

00:00:14.303 --> 00:00:15.700
- No one likes this (beep) holiday!

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.975
- Why do we have to force
a romantic connection

00:00:17.975 --> 00:00:19.228
on a certain day?

00:00:19.228 --> 00:00:21.576
- What's the most romantic
jester you've done,

00:00:21.576 --> 00:00:23.506
or someone has done for
you on Valentine's Day?

00:00:23.506 --> 00:00:25.726
- I snuck into Ariel's room

00:00:25.726 --> 00:00:27.444
and put flowers everywhere,

00:00:27.444 --> 00:00:28.695
this was on her birthday.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.814
- What about for Valentine's Day?

00:00:30.814 --> 00:00:32.694
Men always seem to fail at this,

00:00:32.694 --> 00:00:33.926
it's simple!

00:00:33.926 --> 00:00:36.234
You send presents to her work

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:38.057
to make all her other bitches jealous!

00:00:38.057 --> 00:00:38.890
- Oh, really?

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:40.887
- Valentine's Day isn't about each other!

00:00:40.887 --> 00:00:42.625
It's all about showing everyone else

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:43.616
how much you love each other!

00:00:43.616 --> 00:00:46.476
- Kelsey, we already talk about
how much we love each other,

00:00:46.476 --> 00:00:47.894
all the time anyways,

00:00:47.894 --> 00:00:49.356
and it annoys people!

00:00:49.356 --> 00:00:50.189
Also--

00:00:50.189 --> 00:00:51.922
- Too bad, you don't have a choice.

00:00:51.922 --> 00:00:53.162
What? Also what?

00:00:53.162 --> 00:00:54.374
- She works from home.

00:00:54.374 --> 00:00:55.207
- Oh.

00:00:55.207 --> 00:00:56.882
Ned, it seems like you're
in a weird position

00:00:56.882 --> 00:00:58.432
because you don't really
know what to get her.

00:00:58.432 --> 00:00:59.422
She works from home,

00:00:59.422 --> 00:01:00.255
I'm gonna help you.

00:01:00.255 --> 00:01:01.173
- You are.

00:01:01.173 --> 00:01:04.937
- I'm gonna get a gift for your wife

00:01:04.937 --> 00:01:07.096
for Valentine's Day, from you.

00:01:07.096 --> 00:01:09.048
- So I'm gonna give her a gift from me,

00:01:09.048 --> 00:01:10.494
but it's actually gonna be from you.

00:01:10.494 --> 00:01:11.327
- Yeah!

00:01:11.327 --> 00:01:12.175
- Oh my god, this is very exciting!

00:01:12.175 --> 00:01:13.837
- Let's talk about budget
for Valentine's Day.

00:01:13.837 --> 00:01:16.008
- I really wouldn't want to go above $50.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.829
- So $50 is what we're working with here.

00:01:17.829 --> 00:01:18.662
- Yeah.

00:01:18.662 --> 00:01:20.141
- Okay, here's a trick that I do

00:01:20.141 --> 00:01:22.171
when it's someone else's birthday.

00:01:22.171 --> 00:01:24.992
I buy them a gift that also includes me.

00:01:24.992 --> 00:01:27.122
- I do like that, like experiences.

00:01:27.122 --> 00:01:29.050
- Something you could do together.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:30.750
Oh, wait, I love this!

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:31.740
- I got an idea!

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.407
Hamilton, I went to see
it in New York without her

00:01:34.407 --> 00:01:36.919
and she got really jealous,

00:01:36.919 --> 00:01:38.925
so if I surprise her
with Hamilton tickets--

00:01:38.925 --> 00:01:41.694
- Yeah, but how much money
are you trying to spend?

00:01:41.694 --> 00:01:43.527
- [Both] 1500 dollars!

00:01:44.812 --> 00:01:46.779
- Yikes!
- Oh no!

00:01:46.779 --> 00:01:48.133
- God, this is actually harder

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.311
than I thought it was gonna be.

00:01:49.311 --> 00:01:51.144
Does she like, oh god.

00:01:52.038 --> 00:01:54.081
- I'll just get her the Hamilton tickets.

00:01:54.081 --> 00:01:55.460
- What about if you can read this,

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.120
bring me a glass of wine socks?

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.681
- I'll just take out a second mortgage.

00:01:58.681 --> 00:02:01.198
If you can read this bring
me a second glass of wine.

00:02:01.198 --> 00:02:02.286
- Yeah, and it's on socks,

00:02:02.286 --> 00:02:03.513
so when her feet are up.

00:02:03.513 --> 00:02:04.346
- That's super cute.

00:02:04.346 --> 00:02:05.179
- She likes wine, right?

00:02:05.179 --> 00:02:06.012
- She does like wine!

00:02:06.012 --> 00:02:07.698
- Oh, I got it, I got it.

00:02:07.698 --> 00:02:09.782
What is important about
a Valentine's Day gift?

00:02:09.782 --> 00:02:12.853
It's custom, it's meaningful,

00:02:12.853 --> 00:02:17.332
and it's something that will
remind you of that day forever.

00:02:17.332 --> 00:02:20.593
A custom wine glass would be great.

00:02:20.593 --> 00:02:22.088
- Set of two,

00:02:22.088 --> 00:02:23.214
so that I can drink wine, too!

00:02:23.214 --> 00:02:24.506
- Oh, very good!

00:02:24.506 --> 00:02:27.483
Personalized wine glasses, 19.99!

00:02:27.483 --> 00:02:29.933
- $19, Not bad, not bad!

00:02:29.933 --> 00:02:34.089
- [Kelsey] What if we
got little wine glasses

00:02:34.089 --> 00:02:35.995
with a kiss and a mustache?

00:02:35.995 --> 00:02:36.878
- She would be into that!

00:02:36.878 --> 00:02:40.236
- [Kelsey] Hello, I am looking for

00:02:40.236 --> 00:02:42.736
a custom Valentine's Day gift.

00:02:45.376 --> 00:02:47.043
Thanks so much, Ned.

00:02:48.578 --> 00:02:50.057
Wow, I hope she likes it, I'm nervous.

00:02:50.057 --> 00:02:51.578
- I think she'll like it.

00:02:51.578 --> 00:02:54.618
Ariel, looks like there's
a package here for you.

00:02:54.618 --> 00:02:56.166
Oh, I think you should open it!

00:02:56.166 --> 00:02:57.249
- What is it?

00:02:59.791 --> 00:03:00.753
Oh my gosh!

00:03:00.753 --> 00:03:02.631
It's a big glass that says Ariel!

00:03:02.631 --> 00:03:05.339
(laughter)

00:03:05.339 --> 00:03:06.506
Ariel and Ned!

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.182
That's so cute, honey!

00:03:10.182 --> 00:03:11.369
What are they for?

00:03:11.369 --> 00:03:13.787
- [Ned] It's an early
Valentine's Day present!

00:03:13.787 --> 00:03:15.098
- You!

00:03:15.098 --> 00:03:16.860
- [Ned] I didn't pick them out!

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:17.693
- Oh!

00:03:17.693 --> 00:03:19.124
- [Ned] Kelsey did!

00:03:19.124 --> 00:03:21.324
- Oh, that's adorable!

00:03:21.324 --> 00:03:22.485
Thank you, Kelsey!

00:03:22.485 --> 00:03:25.245
- Kelsey, you are very
good at picking out gifts.

00:03:25.245 --> 00:03:26.078
So that's it!

00:03:26.078 --> 00:03:28.663
Get someone a gift that you can
have an experience together!

00:03:28.663 --> 00:03:29.496
- There you go.

00:03:29.496 --> 00:03:30.491
Like drinking wine.

00:03:30.491 --> 00:03:31.890
- Right.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.079
- Or Hamilton tickets.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:36.171
When in doubt, Hamilton
tickets will make anyone happy.

00:03:36.171 --> 00:03:38.943
- If you have an extra $3000,

00:03:38.943 --> 00:03:40.516
- Paypal it to Ned.
- Hamilton tickets.

00:03:40.516 --> 00:03:43.516
- Oh (laughs) yeah.

